# wasm-pack writes a bare `*` into its output directory, which would silently
# ignore every rebuilt artifact. This package is committed on purpose (README:
# "the WASM package is prebuilt so the app can run without rebuilding Rust"),
# and the root .gitignore already has an explicit `!src/wasm-pkg/` exception,
# so nothing is ignored here on purpose.
#
# If you regenerate the package, `git add -f src/wasm-pkg` to be safe.
